ooking. It is advised for moist cooking, such as chicken cacciatore, braised meat, stewed rabbit, salt cod, etc.<br/></strong>Cooking with Moisture The steam block ensures rapid and thorough cooking. It is advised for moist cooking, such as chicken cacciatore, braised meat, stewed rabbit, salt cod, etc.</p><p><strong>Cooking on a Fan Grill This function is especially quick and deep, and it saves a lot of energy. It can be used for a variety of foods, including game, pork chops, sausages, pork or mixed kebabs, and Roman-style gnocchi.<br/></strong>Cooking on a Fan Grill This function is especially quick and deep, and it saves a lot of energy. It can be used for a variety of foods, including game, pork chops, sausages, pork or mixed kebabs, and Roman-style gnocchi.</p><p><strong>Recommended for quick and deep grilling, browning, and roasting meat in general, fillet, Florentine steak, fish, and even vegetables. Grill Cooking with a Closed Door<br/></strong>Recommended for quick and deep grilling, browning, and roasting meat in general, fillet, Florentine steak, fish, and even vegetables. Grill Cooking with a Closed Door</p><p><strong>Cooking from Above It is especially good for browning and adding the last bit of color to many foods; it is the recommended function for burgers, pork chops, veal steaks, sole, cuttlefish, etc.<br/></strong>Cooking from Above It is especially good for browning and adding the last bit of color to many foods; it is the recommended function for burgers, pork chops, veal steaks, sole, cuttlefish, etc.</p><p><strong>Cooking with Moisture from Above Ideal for browning and giving many foods a final pop of color without sacrificing their tenderness.<br/></strong>Cooking with Moisture from Above Ideal for browning and giving many foods a final pop of color without sacrificing their tenderness.</p><p><strong>Cooking from the Ground Up Pastries (biscuits, meringues, leavened desserts, fruit desserts, etc.) are best cooked using this technique to finish the cooking cycle.<br/></strong>Cooking from the Ground Up Pastries (biscuits, meringues, leavened desserts, fruit desserts, etc.) are best cooked using this technique to finish the cooking cycle.</p><p><strong>Cooking Moist from Below This is the best cooking technique for finishing the cooking cycle while keeping the proper moisture content.<br/></strong>Cooking Moist from Below This is the best cooking technique for finishing the cooking cycle while keeping the proper moisture content.</p><p><strong>Cooking Static Normal Pork chops, sausages, salt cod, braised meat, game, roast veal, meringues and biscuits, baked fruit, etc. can all be cooked in this traditional electric oven function.<br/></strong>Cooking Static Normal Pork chops, sausages, salt cod, braised meat, game, roast veal, meringues and biscuits, baked fruit, etc. can all be cooked in this traditional electric oven function.</p><p><strong>This increases the moisture content of typical static cooking. Cooking with Moist Static<br/></strong>This increases the moisture content of typical static cooking. Cooking with Moist Static</p><p><strong>Cooking with Several Fans This feature enables cooking multiple dishes at once without the smells blending. Lasagna, croissants and brioches, tarts, cakes, etc. can be baked, saving time and electricity.<br/></strong>Cooking with Several Fans This feature enables cooking multiple dishes at once without the smells blending. Lasagna, croissants and brioches, tarts, cakes, etc. can be baked, saving time and electricity.</p><p><strong>Cooking with Several Moist Fans Multiple-fan cooking gains more moisture as a result.<br/></strong>Cooking with Several Moist Fans Multiple-fan cooking gains more moisture as a result.</p><p><strong>Cooking ECO This feature enables you to cook while using much less electricity. Braised meats, white meats, baked pasta, and delicate pastries are just a few examples of foods that benefit from slow roasting when using the ECO function. For fr