, fillet, Florentine steak, fish, and even vegetables.</p><p><strong>Cooking from Above It is especially good for browning and adding the last bit of color to many foods; it is the recommended function for burgers, pork chops, veal steaks, sole, cuttlefish, etc.<br/></strong>Cooking from Above It is especially good for browning and adding the last bit of color to many foods; it is the recommended function for burgers, pork chops, veal steaks, sole, cuttlefish, etc.</p><p><strong>Ideal for browning and giving many foods a final pop of color without sacrificing their tenderness. Cooking with Moisture from Above<br/></strong>Ideal for browning and giving many foods a final pop of color without sacrificing their tenderness. Cooking with Moisture from Above</p><p><strong>Cooking from the Ground Up Pastries (biscuits, meringues, leavened desserts, fruit desserts, etc.) are best cooked using this technique to finish the cooking cycle.<br/></strong>Cooking from the Ground Up Pastries (biscuits, meringues, leavened desserts, fruit desserts, etc.) are best cooked using this technique to finish the cooking cycle.</p><p><strong>Cooking Moist from Below This is the best cooking technique for finishing the cooking cycle while keeping the proper moisture content.<br/></strong>Cooking Moist from Below This is the best cooking technique for finishing the cooking cycle while keeping the proper moisture content.</p><p><strong>Cooking Static Normal Pork chops, sausages, salt cod, braised meat, game, roast veal, meringues and biscuits, baked fruit, etc. can all be cooked in this traditional electric oven function.<br/></strong>Cooking Static Normal Pork chops, sausages, salt cod, braised meat, game, roast veal, meringues and biscuits, baked fruit, etc. can all be cooked in this traditional electric oven function.</p><p><strong>Cooking with Moist Static This increases the moisture content of typical static cooking.<br/></strong>Cooking with Moist Static This increases the moisture conten